 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** The accuracy of the voxel location depends on the resolution of the Reverse Index Texture. If the texture resolution is lower than the volume resolution, aliasing may occur [G].
-*   **Boundaries:** Fragments outside the volume bounds will return invalid or undefined coordinates. A guard should check if $(x_{fb}, y_{fb})$ is within the volume's projected bounds [G].
-*   **Slice Offset:** The slice z-offset must be consistent with the data used to generate the Reverse Index Texture [G]. If the volume is sliced or cropped, the mapping must reflect the current view [G].
